      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-26T16:28:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "is there a way to figure out if concurrent offload is supported?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 80,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 89
      },
      "revId": "b6e8a724e09a4c4e809e6e67686234cf7c988acf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8000cfcb_eccd23ce",
        "filename": "tetheroffload/control/1.0/IOffloadControl.hal",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1062130
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-26T18:08:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the subsequent call to addDownstream() which tries to set concurrent offload on two downstreams, appropriate error will be returned.",
      "parentUuid": "7dbf913b_9b319e5d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 80,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 89
      },
      "revId": "b6e8a724e09a4c4e809e6e67686234cf7c988acf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "341a7629_972deb23",
        "filename": "tetheroffload/control/1.0/IOffloadControl.hal",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-26T22:25:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As a rule of thumb,\n\nif (canDo) {do}\n\nis better than\n\ndo, if (error) {recover}\n\nI understand the confusion as in real life, it is often \"it\u0027s easier to ask for forgiveness than for permission.\" However, this mantra is more often said by shifty people.\n\nSince we\u0027re aware of this being an issue now, why not make it explicit in the interface?",
      "parentUuid": "8000cfcb_eccd23ce",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 80,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 89
      },
      "revId": "b6e8a724e09a4c4e809e6e67686234cf7c988acf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "299efca4_48b1f5cf",
        "filename": "tetheroffload/control/1.0/IOffloadControl.hal",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1062130
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-27T00:07:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "At the very top we define that this API will return a static configuration. Depending on the vendor /hardware implementation, these capabilities can change. For e.g. one device can have wifi from vendor A, and offload HAL from vendor B. whereas another device can have Wifi chipset from vendor B and offload HAL from vendor B. In this case the offload capabilities may be different.\nEven with limited capabilities, framework /client may want to take advantage of hardware offloading for a limited set. Therefore the API is designed to get most juice out of the hardware given there can be variations from soc to soc implementation.",
      "parentUuid": "341a7629_972deb23",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 80,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 89
      },
      "revId": "b6e8a724e09a4c4e809e6e67686234cf7c988acf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ac8b8c19_68a7ed53",
        "filename": "tetheroffload/control/1.0/IOffloadControl.hal",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 73,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-26T16:28:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "what will happen otherwise?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 73,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 73,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "b6e8a724e09a4c4e809e6e67686234cf7c988acf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e74cf6ce_8d3dde2c",
        "filename": "tetheroffload/control/1.0/IOffloadControl.hal",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 73,
      "author": {
        "id": 1062130
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-26T18:08:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Otherwise HAL service must remove all downstreams and upstreams, and perform the clean up by itself. this is just highlighting normal sequence of operation.",
      "parentUuid": "ac8b8c19_68a7ed53",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 73,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 73,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "b6e8a724e09a4c4e809e6e67686234cf7c988acf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
